// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: not re-entrant
// BUG-980: an OVER-REJECTION, pinned on purpose. Both accesses here are READS, and
// POSIX lets a thread hold several concurrent read locks — measured: glibc's default
// (reader-preferring, which is what a zero-initialised pthread_rwlock_t is) returns 0
// for a recursive rdlock, so this program would run.
//
// Refused anyway, for two measured reasons. (1) POSIX leaves it UNSPECIFIED whether a
// recursive rdlock succeeds when a writer is waiting, and under glibc's documented
// PTHREAD_RWLOCK_PREFER_WRITER_NONRECURSIVE_NP it deadlocks — so accepting it makes
// the program's correctness depend on an attribute ZER does not set. (2) The rule
// CANNOT SEE whether the callee reads or writes: FuncSharedTypes records type ids
// only, so "callee reads it too" is not a fact available here, and guessing it is the
// direction that ACCEPTS. The escape is one line — read into a local first.
//
// The fix sketch (a writes-bit per type in the summary) is in docs/limitations.md.
shared(rw) struct S { u32 v; }
S g;
u32 f() { return g.v; }
u32 main() { u32 r = g.v + f(); return r - r; }
